    },
    {
      "id": "blk-part07-1-modules-0016",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 16,
      "source_hash": "0fe4ff8017ca2018267fe7c3d10c331085a0eca7c8c9da985d0cf2424d1eca0b",
      "translation_status": "pending",
      "original": {
        "language": "en",
        "content": "The Python language definition already contains some useful functions, such as the `len` function which returns the length of a string or a list, or the `sum` function which returns the sum of items in a data structure, but they will only get a programmer so far. The Python _standard library_ is a collection of standardised functions and objects, which can be used to expand the expressive power of Python in many ways. We have already used some functions defined in the standard library in previous exercises, for example when calculating square roots."
      },
      "translation": {
        "language": "vi",
        "content": ""
      },
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "blk-part07-1-modules-0017",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 17,
      "source_hash": "d8d90528ca6c0d246c72f69637613ec5779e1f6e295c691f5449b0aa86a903ec",
      "translation_status": "pending",
      "original": {
        "language": "en",
        "content": "The standard library is comprised of _modules_, which contain functions and classes grouped around different themes and functionalities. In this part of the course we will familiarize ourselves with some useful Python modules. We will also learn to write our own modules."
      },
      "translation": {
        "language": "vi",
        "content": ""
      },
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "blk-part07-1-modules-0018",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 18,
      "source_hash": "5dbe97286afed3f7e1aea7f9b1a3f7f2274355dbe6376267e6e07da669ae451a",
      "translation_status": "pending",
      "original": {
        "language": "en",
        "content": "The command `import` makes the contents of the given module accessible in the current program. Let's have a closer look at working with the `math` module. It contains the definitions of some mathematical functions, such as `sqrt` for square root and `log` for logarithm."
      },
      "translation": {
        "language": "vi",
        "content": ""
      },
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "blk-part07-1-modules-0019",
      "type": "code",
      "order": 19,
      "source_hash": "4b04578ff790f0de0b8032a09016bbb76decbc0ceeefd639c255b220ab7d4685",
      "translation_status": "not_applicable",
      "original": {
        "language": "code",
        "content": "import math\n\n# The square root of the number 5\nprint(math.sqrt(5))\n# the base 2 logarithm of the number 8\nprint(math.log(8, 2))"
      },
      "translation": {
        "language": "code",
        "content": "import math\n\n# The square root of the number 5\nprint(math.sqrt(5))\n# the base 2 logarithm of the number 8\nprint(math.log(8, 2))"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "language": "python",
        "code_hash": "4b04578ff790f0de0b8032a09016bbb76decbc0ceeefd639c255b220ab7d4685",
        "length_lines": 6
      }
    },
