    {
      "id": "blk-part07-1-modules-0029",
      "type": "exercise",
      "order": 29,
      "source_hash": "37e86d13587600a5837e95398d99937288e02a4bfef4e83eadd1463073ef6554",
      "translation_status": "pending",
      "original": {
        "language": "en",
        "content": "Please write a function named `hypotenuse(leg1: float, leg2: float)`, which takes the lengths of the two sides adjacent to the right angle of an orthogonal triangle. The function should return the length of the hypotenuse, or the side opposite to the right angle.\n\nYou can use the [Pythagorean theorem](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pythagorean_theorem) to calculate the result. You will need the `sqrt` function from the `math` module.\n\nSome examples:\n\n```python\nprint(hypotenuse(3,4)) # 5.0\nprint(hypotenuse(5,12)) # 13.0\nprint(hypotenuse(1,1)) # 1.4142135623730951\n```"
      },
      "translation": {
        "language": "vi",
        "content": ""
      },
