        "content": "Please familiarize yourself with the Python module `fractions`. Use it to write a function named `fractionate(amount: int)`, which takes the number of parts as its argument. The function should divide the number 1 into as many equal sized fractions as is specified by the argument, and return these in a list.\n\nAn example of the function in action:\n\n```python\nfor p in fractionate(3):\n    print(p)\n\nprint()\n\nprint(fractionate(5))\n```\n\n<sample-output>\n\n1/3\n1/3\n1/3\n\n[Fraction(1, 5), Fraction(1, 5), Fraction(1, 5), Fraction(1, 5), Fraction(1, 5)]\n\n</sample-output>"
